Overview:   &nbsp;

Guidepoint’s Business Development teams are passionate about expanding our reach with both new and existing clients. We support Guidepoint’s full suite of service offerings - from expert interviews and surveys to insights and research solutions - helping clients stay informed and make better business decisions. Our teams focus on building long-term partnerships and delivering tailored solutions that maximize client value. &nbsp;

What You’ll Do:   &nbsp;

• Drive outbound prospecting efforts to identify, qualify, and develop new business opportunities across Southeast Asia corporate accounts &nbsp;

• Build and manage relationships with existing strategic accounts to identify growth, retention, and cross-selling opportunities across Guidepoint’s service offerings &nbsp;

• Lead the end-to-end sales cycle, including client meetings, commercial discussions, proposal development, contracting, and delivery coordination &nbsp;

• Partner closely with Client Service teams to ensure high-quality execution and strong client outcomes &nbsp;

• Achieve designated business development, revenue, and account growth targets through disciplined pipeline management and commercial execution &nbsp;

• Conduct client feedback and account review meetings to strengthen relationships and uncover new opportunities &nbsp;

• Support the development of marketing materials, client presentations, and go-to-market initiatives for new products and solutions &nbsp;

• Develop a strong understanding of primary research methodologies, industry trends, competitor landscape, and corporate clients’ strategic decision-making processes  &nbsp;

What You Have:   &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university &nbsp;

• Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English &nbsp;

• Strong consultative selling capabilities with a solution-oriented mindset &nbsp;

• 5+ years of professional experience, including at least 3+ years in KPI- and metrics-driven business development or sales roles within insights, research, consulting, or information services industries &nbsp;

• Experience managing corporate clients across multiple sectors in Southeast Asia markets preferred &nbsp;

• Proven ability to engage and influence senior stakeholders and high-profile clients &nbsp;

• Strong commercial acumen, relationship management, and client-facing presentation skills &nbsp;

• Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial, and results-oriented team environment &nbsp;

• Self-driven, resilient, and highly collaborative with strong ownership mentality &nbsp;

What We Offer:   &nbsp;

• Competitive compensation&nbsp;

• Employee medical coverage&nbsp;

• Central office location&nbsp;

• Entrepreneurial environment, autonomy, and fast decisions&nbsp;

• Casual work environment&nbsp;

About Guidepoint &nbsp;

Guidepoint powers end-to-end research workflows for the world’s best research teams. &nbsp;

Backed by a global network of more than 2 million experts and over 1,600 employees , Guidepoint delivers real-time access to expertise, primary research, and actionable knowledge that help organizations make informed decisions. Through consultations, surveys, events, proprietary content, and AI-enabled tools, we support every stage of the decision-making process-from developing hypotheses and gathering insights to validating assumptions and building conviction for critical decisions. &nbsp;

At Guidepoint, our success relies on the diversity of our employees, experts, and clients, which enables us to foster meaningful connections and a broad range of perspectives. We are committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment where individuals of all backgrounds, identities, and experiences can contribute and succeed. &nbsp;

